WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.869
The paper makes four main contributions.

00:00:03.949 --> 00:00:07.818
First, it introduces MeZO,

00:00:07.898 --> 00:00:11.768
a memory-efficient zeroth-order optimizer that
adapts classical zeroth-order SGD to operate in place,

00:00:11.848 --> 00:00:15.717
so fine-tuning costs no more memory than inference.

00:00:15.797 --> 00:00:19.666
Second, through comprehensive experiments across
masked and autoregressive models,

00:00:19.746 --> 00:00:23.615
scales up to sixty-six billion parameters, and
classification, multiple-choice,

00:00:23.695 --> 00:00:27.565
and generation tasks,

00:00:27.645 --> 00:00:31.514
it shows MeZO matches full backpropagation
fine-tuning while using far less memory.

00:00:31.594 --> 00:00:35.463
Third,

00:00:35.543 --> 00:00:39.412
it demonstrates compatibility with
parameter-efficient methods like LoRA and prefix tuning,

00:00:39.492 --> 00:00:43.362
and the ability to optimize non-differentiable
objectives such as accuracy or F1.

00:00:43.442 --> 00:00:47.311
Fourth,

00:00:47.391 --> 00:00:51.260
it supplies theory explaining why MeZO converges
quickly despite the enormous parameter count.
